    skos:definition "a pulse, the *Ervm lens*, the seeds of which are amyllaceous and nutritious, but difficult of digestion. It is much used as food in southern countries, and the meal forms the base of a popular substance vended under the name of *Revallenta Arabica*. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 238]"@en ;
